2026-01-14 12:32:48 | INFO | "./webui\batch_video_generator.py:98": generate_single_video - task.start completed with result: {'videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\cd6b2778-722c-4588-98e5-d32ea5e12e4f\\final-1.mp4'], 'combined_videos': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\cd6b2778-722c-4588-98e5-d32ea5e12e4f\\combined-1.mp4'], 'script': 'When you have diabetes, staying hydrated is absolutely crucial, and yes, drinking plenty of water is generally a fantastic idea. Think of water as your ally; it helps your kidneys flush out excess sugar from your bloodstream, a process that becomes even more vital when your blood glucose levels are elevated. This diligent hydration can significantly reduce the strain on your kidneys and contribute to better overall metabolic control, potentially preventing those frustrating fluctuations in your energy levels. Don\'t underestimate the power of a simple glass of water to make a real difference in how you feel and manage your diabetes day to day. However, "a lot" needs a little clarification, especially if you\'re experiencing uncontrolled diabetes or symptoms like extreme thirst. In those instances, while water is still your best friend, you might be peeing out a significant amount of fluid due to high blood sugar, which can lead to dehydration if you don\'t replenish it. It\'s also worth noting that for individuals with certain kidney conditions that can sometimes co-exist with diabetes, excessive fluid intake might need to be monitored by your doctor. The key is to listen to your body\'s thirst signals and aim for consistent, balanced hydration throughout the day rather than chugging gallons at once. Ultimately, for most people living with diabetes, increased water intake is a safe and beneficial practice that can actively support your health management goals. It’s a natural, calorie-free way to help your body function optimally and combat some of the physical challenges diabetes can present. If you\'re ever in doubt about the right amount of fluids for your specific situation, a quick chat with your healthcare provider or a registered dietitian can provide personalized guidance, ensuring you\'re hydrating effectively and safely on your diabetes journey.', 'terms': ['diabetes', 'water intake', 'kidney function', 'thirsty', 'sugar-free drink'], 'audio_file': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\cd6b2778-722c-4588-98e5-d32ea5e12e4f\\audio.mp3', 'audio_duration': 108, 'subtitle_path': 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\tasks\\cd6b2778-722c-4588-98e5-d32ea5e12e4f\\subtitle.srt', 'materials': ['C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-83f3f208089985010cb49071d86c6ac7.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-b2c578574069027a9b53a00cbbb6dd50.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-a4144b0bcc24bec3ae0f8dd430fa4f4b.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-1c64f1087f2fe315f71ab74739ca7032.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-c18d413aefb42e4b5e6b3963a3cd6b33.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-a1b506a0dd0233bc79b495bc43769540.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-045a4f48d39d6a3669612cc559c76016.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-3da514b55575d5cc6ca2df4785b20263.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-1fd20b13908f1161aa9b3659dafd40bf.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-4ad1fe2e5237dac10069da62936c0c79.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-e2cda2c0f5ff14c5b010c9900dee8d8b.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-0d67b2ff4069ed704c6eceb4d32f2c8a.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-8e9fcc72194461d27c033f3a17fbe5bc.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\cache_videos/vid-4b8aee5f77d0875dce74ba80583d7ef0.mp4', 'C:\\Users\\dev\\youtube-auto\\storage\\c