2026-01-27 22:20:44 | DEBUG | "./app\services\task.py:35": generate_script - video script: 
Did you know that the seeds of diabetes are hidden in the foods we eat mindlessly every day? If you succumb to sweet temptations and eat without restraint, repeated blood sugar spikes can exhaust your pancreas, leading to insulin resistance. Beware of refined carbohydrates like sugar-laden drinks, white bread, and instant noodles, as they are the main culprits that cause your blood sugar to spike rapidly. Seemingly ordinary bread or cookies, and a single cup of coffee laden with sweet syrup, can instantly push you over your daily recommended sugar intake. High-sugar fruit juices are no different; they are simply concentrated blocks of sugar without any fiber. These foods, with their high glycemic index (GI), are rapidly absorbed into your body, overworking your blood vessels and potentially becoming a fast track to diabetes. Many dangerous foods don't even taste particularly sweet. Various sauces like ketchup and barbecue sauce, surprisingly many processed foods, and even cereals that are easily mistaken for health foods, contain enormous amounts of hidden sugar. These hidden sugars burden our liver, are stored as fat, contribute to chronic inflammation, and impair insulin function. Now, it's time to think twice before you eat and develop the habit of checking the nutrition facts label on the back of food products. You must choose wisely for the long-term health of your body, rather than for short-term pleasure. Keep in mind that mindless eating habits can make your future self sick, so start making small changes to your diet today.
