## generating video script
2026-01-29 12:10:50 | DEBUG | "./app\services\task.py:35": generate_script - video script: 
Don't let nighttime urination disturb your restful sleep any longer. Strictly limit your fluid intake starting 3 hours before bedtime, and in the evening, you must avoid caffeine and alcohol. By cutting out diuretic beverages, you can reduce your trips to the bathroom at night and regain a peaceful night's sleep. Bladder training is also essential. Gradually increase the time you hold your urine during the day to expand your bladder capacity, and strengthen your pelvic floor muscles with regular Kegel exercises. These small habits will remarkably improve your bladder control and provide comfort throughout the night.

Optimizing your sleep environment is also important. Since your urine volume can increase if your body gets cold, keep your pajamas and bedding warm. It's advisable to help blood circulation with light stretching before bed, and to boost physical vitality with regular exercise while managing stress.

If nighttime urination persists despite all these efforts, don't hesitate to consult a urologist. There might be an underlying medical cause, and early diagnosis and treatment can significantly improve your quality of life. Now it's time to break free from the discomfort of nighttime bathroom trips and regain the joy of refreshing, deep sleep!
