 stress is a silent enemy that can wreak havoc on your body, potentially raising cholesterol levels and increasing inflammation, so make prioritizing stress-reducing activities non-negotiable. Incorporate daily practices like mindful meditation, calming deep breathing exercises, or restorative time spent in nature to soothe your nervous system and bring balance. If you smoke, quitting is arguably the most impactful step you can take for your cardiovascular system; smoking severely damages blood vessel linings and accelerates the buildup of arterial plaque, making cessation an absolute game-changer for reclaiming your heart health. These conscious, holistic choices create an optimal internal environment where your body thrives, naturally pushing high cholesterol out of the picture and safeguarding your future without relying on a single medication.', 'video_id': None, 'type': 'shorts', 'language': 'en-US', 'upload_error': None, 'file_size': 195533623, 'auto_upload_requested': True}
